Still, some basics may be helpful. Adding a new paragraph is as simple as pressing enter twice:

No need for multiple \verb!\\!, \verb!\newline!s, or \verb!\par!.
You can adjust the indentation and spacing of the paragraph using\\
\verb!\setlength{\parindent}{0pt}!\\
and\\
\verb!\setlength{\parskip}{0.75\baselineskip}!.

Citations are input using BibLaTeX, e.g.,\\
\verb!\textcite{sigfridsson}!: \textcite{sigfridsson}\\
\verb!\autocite{aristotle:physics}!: \autocite{aristotle:physics}.\\
The bibliography is printed at the end of this section using\\
\verb!\printbibliography!.

%</crs1|bama1|bama2|rp1|rp2|phd1|phd2|art1>
%<*crs1|bama1|bama2|rp1|rp2|phd1|phd2>
