\section{Loading the theme and theme options}
\begin{frame}[section]
  \sectionpage
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}
  {Using the beamer theme}

  The \texttt{ugent} beamer theme is distributed by CTAN. It
  should be installed with your \textrm{\TeX{}} distribution by default.

  You can load the package in your preamble as:

  \begin{codesnippet}
    \cmd{documentclass}\{beamer\}\\
    \cmd{usetheme}[<theme options>]\{ugent\}
  \end{codesnippet}

  \heading{Remarks}
  \begin{itemize}
  \item The theme's default aspect ratio is $16\times 9$, but you might be able to override it by
    re-loading the \texttt{beamerposter} package with custom width and height, and
    redefining \cmd{@PW} (page width), \cmd{@PH} (page height), and \cmd{gridunit}.
    This is not officially supported.
  \item Only \texttt{dutch} and \texttt{english} are officially supported through the \texttt{language} option.
  \end{itemize}
\end{frame}

