  {Theme options}{}
  The following theme options may come in handy --
    see also the \texttt{ugentdocs} documentation:
  \begin{description}
  \item[\texttt{faculty}] to set your own faculty's colours and logos (can be empty)\\
  \item[\texttt{campus}] to set the campus for the UGent logo. One of \texttt{ugent},
    \texttt{gugc}, or \texttt{kortrijk}.
  \item[\texttt{neutralcolors}] to disable your faculty colours and use the
  standard UGent colours
  \item[\texttt{colormodel}] to set the colour model. Select \texttt{rgb}
    colour encoding for projecting (default) or \texttt{cmyk} for printing.
  \item[\texttt{secnums}] to enable (\texttt{true}) or disable (\texttt{false})
    displaying of section numbers in the frames or TOC.
  \end{description}

\end{graphicframe}

\begin{frame}[t]
{Colours}
{What a wonderful world}

\heading{Standard colours}\\
  You can select the theme colours using:\\
  \textcolor{ugent@main}{Main colour}:
    can be specified as \textrm{\LaTeX}-colour \emph{ugent@main}\\
  \textcolor{ugent@accent}{Accent colour}:
    can be specified as \textrm{\LaTeX}-colour \emph{ugent@accent}\\
  \textcolor{ugent@faculty}{Faculty colour}:
    can be specified as \textrm{\LaTeX}-colour
    \emph{ugent@faculty}

\heading{Alert}\\
  You can use \alert{\cmd{alert{}}} to grab the attention of the
  user. It will typeset your content in \alert{yellow}.
\end{frame}

